Wd5lQwXQfW1yecbF25d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06de9a2827572a23c1df0e999a6d8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure\",\n    \"title\": \"Initial instance collection failure unknown freshness and attempted state lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTests cover a collection failure only after a successful snapshot. They do not defend the stronger first-observation invariant: an instance that has never succeeded is unknown, never fresh or stale, while still showing the failed attempt.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter the first collection attempt fails for an instance with no prior snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:00.096Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: view.go:208-213 (instanceView), view.go:160 (classifyFreshness), templates/instance.html:18 (\\\"Waiting for first observation\\\"). Behaviors: when an instance has never completed a successful collection (e.g. host unreachable or binary failure on first launch), Canopy must maintain its freshness as \\\"unknown\\\" (never \\\"stale\\\" or \\\"fresh\\\"), set Reachable: false, record LastObserved with prefix \\\"attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e\\\", surface the failure in Errors, and render the \\\"Waiting for first observation\\\" card. Failing example: configure an instance whose collector fails immediately on the first attempt without any prior successful snapshot; today TestRefreshRetainsLastSuccessfulSnapshotOnFailure in app_test.go only tests failure after an initial success (transitioning to \\\"stale\\\"), leaving the initial-failure path (view.go:210) untested. Acceptance: a Builder adds a regression test in app_test.go asserting that after an initial refresh failure, app.state(id) has Snapshot == nil, instanceView has Freshness: \\\"unknown\\\", Reachable: false, LastObserved prefixed with \\\"attempted \\\", Errors containing the collector error, and instance.html rendering the waiting-title card. Observed: view.go:210 sets \\\"attempted \\\" when Snapshot is nil and LastAttempt is non-zero, but grep shows \\\"attempted\\\" is never asserted in any test file. Required: a regression test in app_test.go for initial instance collection failure. Proposed test-work: add an app/view regression test proving an instance failing its initial collection reports unknown freshness, attempted timestamp, and the waiting card.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:26:41.534Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:29:23.983Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"ask: Implementation and checks are complete at f93e178 on forest/canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure/first-failure-proof; PR https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/pull/11. Focused regression, all Go tests, and go vet pass. This executive session has no Runner FOREST_RUN_ID, so it cannot publish authorized Builder review-request evidence. An authorized Builder Run must adopt this exact branch, validate/rebase if needed, and publish forest.review-request.v2 for tracker powder. Do not treat the PR or raw branch push as Gate approval or job completion.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:31:26.472Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"text\": \"answer: Executive recovery complete: PR #11 closed and remote forest branch deleted. No review-request evidence was created. Implementation is preserved in the local ref executive/initial-collection-failure-preserved at f93e178. A normal Builder may select this job, inspect/cherry-pick that commit into its own fresh forest branch if useful, rerun checks, and publish through the authorized Runner Gate. Do not treat prior PR or checks as approval.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTests cover a collection failure only after a successful snapshot. They do not defend the stronger first-observation invariant: an instance that has never succeeded is unknown, never fresh or stale, while still showing the failed attempt.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter the first collection attempt fails for an instance with no prior snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:54.638Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:31:26.472Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": true\n    }\n  }\n]\nEXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550424313},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01a06de9a86b7a90a2375bd44da276e7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"gh issue list --repo misty-step/canopy --label \"forest:ready\" --state open --limit 20; echo \"EXIT:$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":1645,"output":74,"cacheRead":11761,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13480,"cost":{"input":0.00156275,"output":0.000296,"cacheRead":0.0018817600000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00374051}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788550424314,"responseId":"gen-1788550424-Ozne10OAtjaQF9xtXZVk","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06de9a86b7a90a2375bd44da276e7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"EXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550425855},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"Q-PaDgEys0L7K4FcTzHq2HHk9iksM6p0Jt33xYm4wBF8A1Gd-8K9znFMYnQa0dV4_NttkzINetkzHt3X_uMqjJl1sCn09xQSdKdnFEl47Ur7fAw9ncIrxVNJgFbJ9d-7PWU3SYw6FE1p9MGYKC04egb4ej_Io7X7lnAiYoZcIg_D6w71dpFDkAnkh9ViWb6Cyb5xzFzwYsEorXHs2tWY-ZJFMh6PijrI3xgFKgloAfsu53WS50DYRWjv73yHjO