or snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\",\"repo\":\"misty-step/canopy\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"lease\":{\"agent\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"principal\":\"none\",\"until\":\"2026-09-04T23:33:53.108Z\"},\"ask\":null,\"proof\":null,\"abandoned\":false,\"notes\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T18:59:00.096Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: view.go:208-213 (instanceView), view.go:160 (classifyFreshness), templates/instance.html:18 (\\\"Waiting for first observation\\\"). Behaviors: when an instance has never completed a successful collection (e.g. host unreachable or binary failure on first launch), Canopy must maintain its freshness as \\\"unknown\\\" (never \\\"stale\\\" or \\\"fresh\\\"), set Reachable: false, record LastObserved with prefix \\\"attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e\\\", surface the failure in Errors, and render the \\\"Waiting for first observation\\\" card. Failing example: configure an instance whose collector fails immediately on the first attempt without any prior successful snapshot; today TestRefreshRetainsLastSuccessfulSnapshotOnFailure in app_test.go only tests failure after an initial success (transitioning to \\\"stale\\\"), leaving the initial-failure path (view.go:210) untested. Acceptance: a Builder adds a regression test in app_test.go asserting that after an initial refresh failure, app.state(id) has Snapshot == nil, instanceView has Freshness: \\\"unknown\\\", Reachable: false, LastObserved prefixed with \\\"attempted \\\", Errors containing the collector error, and instance.html rendering the waiting-title card. Observed: view.go:210 sets \\\"attempted \\\" when Snapshot is nil and LastAttempt is non-zero, but grep shows \\\"attempted\\\" is never asserted in any test file. Required: a regression test in app_test.go for initial instance collection failure. Proposed test-work: add an app/view regression test proving an instance failing its initial collection reports unknown freshness, attempted timestamp, and the waiting card.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:26:41.534Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\"text\":\"took\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:29:23.983Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\"text\":\"ask: Implementation and checks are complete at f93e178 on forest/canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure/first-failure-proof; PR https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/pull/11. Focused regression, all Go tests, and go vet pass. This executive session has no Runner FOREST_RUN_ID, so it cannot publish authorized Builder review-request evidence. An authorized Builder Run must adopt this exact branch, validate/rebase if needed, and publish forest.review-request.v2 for tracker powder. Do not treat the PR or raw branch push as Gate approval or job completion.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:31:26.472Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"text\":\"answer: Executive recovery complete: PR #11 closed and remote forest branch deleted. No review-request evidence was created. Implementation is preserved in the local ref executive/initial-collection-failure-preserved at f93e178. A normal Builder may select this job, inspect/cherry-pick that commit into its own fresh forest branch if useful, rerun checks, and publish through the authorized Runner Gate. Do not treat prior PR or checks as approval.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:33:53.108Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"took\"}],\"created_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\"promotions\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nTests cover a collection failure only after a successful snapshot. They do not defend the stronger first-observation invariant: an instance that has never succeeded is unknown, never fresh or stale, while still showing the failed attempt.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter the first collection attempt fails for an instance with no prior snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T18:58:54.638Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:33:53.108Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\nEXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550433152},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"Q-PaDgGlxOuCa8b1rO_PL-cOhoIMxJXsI1qDFFVnYIx2XUAQyZxpNjHigHhMk